{
  "version": "1",
  "description": "Layer-band attention patching as ONE document. A band patches the complete attention_output at every layer in the span during the SAME forward pass, and the sweep language genuinely cannot express that - one start-layer value would have to expand into five or ten dependent writes, and a sweep expands one axis into independent points. 'intervened_models' is the mechanism that can: each entry names the set of writes in force for one forward, so several bands - overlapping ones included - are several entries over ONE table of per-layer writes. That is one model load for every band, not one per band; a verified A3B document carried 41 sites, 40 writes and 67 intervened_models (every 5- and 10-layer band of a 40-layer tower) in a single campaign. Scale this by extending the sites/reads/writes tables one entry per layer and adding one intervened_models entry per band; nothing else changes. Note the two widths here share their writes: band10_L10 is band5_L10's and band5_L15's writes together, and each write is authored once.",
